"I'm placing an ad for a housekeeper."

00:00:06.055 --> 00:00:09.000
"Hello? Are your kids well behaved?"

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.005
"You remind me of someone.."

00:00:16.965 --> 00:00:19.000
"You will follow a schedule."

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.955
"Those who do not follow the schedule will be punished.."

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.320
"We've got to dial 911 now!"

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:36.960
"H̷͉̠͒͠e̸̩̹̻͗̿͠͝ľ̸̗͈̘̩l̷̳̞͓͊o̴̖͈͌͆͛̓ !"

00:00:44.245 --> 00:00:45.445
Hello, internet!

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:47.400
Welcome to FILM THEORY!

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:50.095
removing the nostalgia glasses

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:53.205
from your eyes and grinding them under our digital video heel every week

00:00:53.205 --> 00:00:55.460
On the chopping block today, the beloved 1993

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:58.120
family comedy, Mrs. Doubtfire.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:01.080
Which, if you grew up in the 90's, you'll

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:04.135
understand that 'beloved' is an understatement.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:07.200
This thing was a STAPLE in everyone's VHS

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.180
collections. A yearly, if not daily watch

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:13.260
for a lot of kids around the country. Like most of Robin William's movies

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:19.200
it was an instant classic. Simultaneously hilarious and heart-warming in that unique way that only he could do.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.485
For those of you who haven't seen the film before,

00:01:21.485 --> 00:01:24.465
here's the brief overview: Robin Williams, AKA Daniel

00:01:24.465 --> 00:01:27.415
Hillard, is a talented voice actor living with his wife Miranda,

00:01:27.415 --> 00:01:30.445
and three kids in San Francisco, California

00:01:30.445 --> 00:01:32.925
Early on in the film Miranda files for divorce after Daniel

00:01:32.925 --> 00:01:35.735
throws a wild birthday party for their son.

00:01:35.735 --> 00:01:38.075
Because he doesn't have a regular job or place to live, the

00:01:38.075 --> 00:01:41.085
family court grants primary custody to Miranda,

00:01:41.085 --> 00:01:44.105
only allowing Daniel to have visitation rights for a few hours every week.

00:01:44.105 --> 00:01:47.080
Daniel, devastated that he can't see his kids everyday,

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:49.400
does what any normal parent would do:

00:01:49.405 --> 00:01:51.600
use professional-grade prosthetics to disguise himself

00:01:51.605 --> 00:01:54.685
as an elderly British woman in order to get himself hired as his children's nanny

00:01:54.685 --> 00:01:57.565
As you can imagine, hilarity ensues as Daniel struggles

00:01:57.565 --> 00:02:00.585
to maintain his double life. But what you were really laughing at

00:02:00.585 --> 00:02:03.345
weren't the antics of a dedicated loving father,

00:02:03.345 --> 00:02:06.205
but really the machinations of a morally

00:02:06.205 --> 00:02:08.375
bankrupt criminal. Oh sure,

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:11.255
he opposes advertising cigarettes to children. (Daniel) Pudgy the parrot has a

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:13.860
cigarette shoved into his mouth is morally irresponsible

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:14.895
Millions of kids see this

00:02:14.895 --> 00:02:17.815
cartoon as like sending each one of them a pack of cigarettes and saying, "Light up!"

00:02:17.815 --> 00:02:20.105
(MatPat) Then gives this heartfelt speech at the end of the film

00:02:20.105 --> 00:02:23.385
(Daniel) In regards to my behaviour, I can only plead insanity, because

00:02:23.475 --> 00:02:26.415
ever since my children were born, the moment I looked at them

00:02:26.415 --> 00:02:29.025
I was crazy about them. (MatPat) But I'm here today to EXPOSE Daniel,

00:02:29.025 --> 00:02:31.985
not just for his crimes, but also his behaviour, that quite

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:35.500
honestly should warn in seeing a mental health professional. So it's time to

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:38.800
CRACK open those law books and find out whether Daniel Hillard will be exchanging his

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:41.540
dress and wig for an orange jumpsuit and um..

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:44.695
not dropping the soap. Before we begin we have to determine which laws

00:02:44.695 --> 00:02:47.595
to use when judging Daniel's actions throughout the film.

00:02:47.595 --> 00:02:50.465
Though it's not officially stated, Mrs. Doubtfire

00:02:50.465 --> 00:02:53.465
is known to take place in San Francisco, California. Multiple scenes show

00:02:53.465 --> 00:02:56.565
San Francisco landmarks, and the climactic scene of the film

00:02:56.565 --> 00:02:59.785
takes place at Bridges restaurant, which is a real-life establishment

00:02:59.785 --> 00:03:02.825
located in Bay Area. Therefore, the United States,

00:03:02.825 --> 00:03:05.885
the State of California, San Francisco county, and

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:07.265
the city of San Francisco will all

00:03:07.265 --> 00:03:10.405
have jurisdiction over Daniel. Additionally, the movie

00:03:10.405 --> 00:03:13.275
was created in 1993, so I'm gonna try to only look at

00:03:13.275 --> 00:03:16.055
laws that were on the books around that time.

00:03:16.055 --> 00:03:19.015
So now that we know which laws are applicable, let's start going through

00:03:19.015 --> 00:03:21.805
the film. From the opening moment,

00:03:21.805 --> 00:03:24.705
Daniel's self-destructive habits are clearly on display.

00:03:24.705 --> 00:03:27.560
The first scene has him actively sabotaging an important

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:30.660
voice-over job. (Guy) This session is costing the studio thousands of

00:03:30.665 --> 00:03:33.680
dollars. You wanna play Gandhi, then do it on somebody else's time!

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:35.540
If you leave, you're not coming back in.

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:36.880
(Daniel, as Gandhi)
Then I've got to do...

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:37.900
...what I've got to do.

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:39.760
(MatPat) And he's not wrong to walk out of this job,

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:42.515
but at this point he chooses to spiral downward

00:03:42.515 --> 00:03:45.545
even further in his self-destructive habits, by throwing a

00:03:45.545 --> 00:03:48.475
blatantly out-of-control party for his kids.

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:51.625
A party that he clearly recognises as against the wishes of his wife

00:03:51.625 --> 00:03:53.060
(Son) Party? (Daniel) YES!

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:54.880
(Daughter) No! Mom said you couldn't have one

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.200
because of your report card.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:57.935
(Daniel) Mom's not gonna be home for another

00:03:57.935 --> 00:03:58.935
four hours, is she?

00:03:59.355 --> 00:04:02.445
(MatPat) A party that also happens to be highly illegal.

00:04:02.445 --> 00:04:06.000
(Policeman) Are you aware that it's illegal to possess animals of a barnyard nature in a residential area?

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:08.580
while also responding to a noise ordinance violation.

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:09.760
(MatPat) How illegal?

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:11.320
Well, funny enough, I couldn't find anything about

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:14.600
possession of barnyard animals in a residential neighborhood on the books.

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:16.560
However, I did find

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:20.620
Article 1, Section 37, Clause C of the San Francisco Public Health Code.

00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:23.200
Which prohibits the possession of hooved animals

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:24.500
within a residential district.

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:26.520
Not exact, but pretty darn close.

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:29.560
Both goats and horses, which are seen during the scene,

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:31.600
would be a direct violation of this statute.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:36.020
Resulting in a punishment of about $100 and approximately 30 days in county jail.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:39.180
Since this would be his first offense, the jail time would probably be waived.

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:42.340
And for the noise violation, Daniel would only be fined another 100 bucks

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:47.000
as specified by Section 291y of the San Francisco Police Code.

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:48.720
Regardless, let's recap.

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:50.240
In the first seven minutes,

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:54.060
the hero of the movie has shown himself to be self-sabotaging in both his job,

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.960
and in his relationship.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:59.620
As well as be liable for at least $200 in criminal fines and possibly

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:01.280
30 days in prison.

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:05.460
Sure, the movie frames Daniel as the "Cool Dad" who's being henpecked by his

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:06.880
stick in the mud, workaholic wife,

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:09.660
but the subtext here is that we have an unhappy man

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:11.640
who rebounds from misfortune by

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:16.480
engaging in even more self-destructive behaviors that he knows are wrong!

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:19.175
(Wife) Don't you dare make me have to be the monster here, Daniel!

00:05:19.175 --> 00:05:21.540
You have all the fun and I get whatever's left over!

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:24.180
Why am I the only one that feels there has to be rule?

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:26.940
(MatPat) And that spiral just continues throughout the movie.

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:29.860
This opening scene results in Miranda getting a divorce from Daniel

00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:31.940
and her winning sole custody over the kids.

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:34.820
Because he doesn't have a home or any form of employment,

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:38.080
Daniel is only allowed to have visitation rights on Saturdays.

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:39.845
(Daniel) Every Saturday, it's one day a week.

00:05:39.845 --> 00:05:40.760
That's not enough.

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:42.220
(MatPat) Unhappy with the court's ruling,

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:44.455
Daniel devises the plan to disguise himself

00:05:44.455 --> 00:05:47.500
as a British nanny in order to trick Miranda into hiring him

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:49.705
so he can spend more time with the kids.

00:05:49.705 --> 00:05:52.240
All this, while Miranda finds herself a new boyfriend,

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:52.845
Stu.

00:05:52.965 --> 00:05:54.885
And this, is where the plot of the movie,

00:05:54.885 --> 00:05:57.500
and Daniel's "crime spree" truly begin.

00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:01.365
You see, I know it was a common trope of movies, especially in the 90's

00:06:01.365 --> 00:06:03.140
to portray step-parents as evil,

00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:04.155
But unlike other films,

00:06:04.155 --> 00:06:07.595
Stu actually makes an effort to bond with these kids,

00:06:07.595 --> 00:06:10.165
and seems very genuine about his relationship with them.

00:06:10.165 --> 00:06:13.355
One of his buddies even asks why he's dating someone with "baggage"

00:06:13.355 --> 00:06:15.040
and he responds by saying that they're,

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:16.900
(Stu) Terrific kids, and I'm crazy about them.

00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:19.960
(MatPat) So what does Daniel do to this unusually good-natured boyfriend?

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:21.675
He takes advantage of his generosity,

00:06:21.675 --> 00:06:22.880
vandalizes his car,

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:24.100
and then nearly murders him.

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:26.140
You know, family-friendly comedy stuff!

00:06:26.140 --> 00:06:27.980
It's okay to kill your romantic rival

00:06:27.980 --> 00:06:29.760
and kids' possible stepdad,

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:32.220
In one scene, Daniel, dressed as Mrs. Doubtfire,

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:34.140
takes the ornament off of Stu's Mercedes.

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:35.220
Since he, quote,

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:38.240
endquote.

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:41.980
It would technically be considered vandalism by the California Penal Code,

00:06:41.980 --> 00:06:46.660
and would result in a $1000 fine and potentially another year in county jail.

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:49.660
California's not messin' around, you American Vandals.

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:52.420
Never seen that show, but Phil DeFranco says it's good. I might have to check it out.

00:06:52.420 --> 00:06:53.640
In a later scene, Daniel,

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:55.500
once again disguised as Doubtfire,

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:58.480
is at a bar and hears Stu criticize him as a negligent father.

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:00.460
(Stu) What can I say, Ron? The guy's a loser.

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:03.500
(MatPat) Daniel responds by throwing a blindsided lime at Stu.

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:04.965
(Daniel as Doubtfire) I saw it!

00:07:04.965 --> 00:07:06.520
Some angry member of the kitchen staff,

00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:07.900
it was a run-by fruiting!

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:10.520
Believe it or not, this too could be considered a crime.

00:07:10.520 --> 00:07:13.895
A district attorney would likely classify it as battery.

00:07:13.895 --> 00:07:14.720
Defined as, quote:

00:07:19.425 --> 00:07:24.280
Which adds another $2000 fine and potentially 6 months of county jail time

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:26.300
to Daniel's growing rap sheet.

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:27.980
But all of this is small potatoes,

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:29.720
or should I say "small limes"

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:33.080
when compared to Daniel's most violent crime of the entire film,

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:35.575
The near-murder of Stu.

00:07:35.575 --> 00:07:37.580
The movie culminates in a final, chaotic scene

00:07:37.580 --> 00:07:40.820
where Daniel has to keep shifting back and forth between his two identities.

00:07:40.820 --> 00:07:42.100
Amongst all this mayhem,

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:44.695
Daniel takes the time to steal a chef's jacket,

00:07:44.695 --> 00:07:45.920
sneak into the kitchen,

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:48.040
and then add pepper to Stu's shrimp,

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:51.640
despite being very well aware that Stu is allergic to pepper.

00:07:51.640 --> 00:07:53.145
(Stu) I'll have the John (inaudible).

00:07:53.145 --> 00:07:55.385
--And make mine not-spicy, I'm allergic to pepper.

00:07:55.385 --> 00:07:57.625
(MatPat) When the food is served, Stu begins to eat it,

00:07:57.625 --> 00:08:00.260
Stu immediately has himself an allergic reaction.

00:08:00.260 --> 00:08:01.940
Not a funny sort of reaction,

00:08:01.940 --> 00:08:03.480
a dangerous one.

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:05.700
Daniel recognizes his mistake, exclaiming,

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:07.340
(Daniel) Oh no, I killed the bastard!

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:09.815
(MatPat) --before successfully giving him the Heimlich maneuver.

00:08:09.815 --> 00:08:11.780
Now, clearly, this is a crime.

00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:13.840
But, what sort of crime is it?

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:17.080
Well, if Stu had died, like he was on the verge of,

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:20.120
it would have been tried as voluntary manslaughter. 
In which:

00:08:25.180 --> 00:08:25.935
In this case,

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:29.160
Daniel sprinkling the pepper was meant to be a harmful prank,

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:29.960
ITS JUST A PRANK, BRO

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.535
But at no point did he intend to kill Stu

00:08:32.540 --> 00:08:35.080
as evidenced by him doing the Heimlich to save him.

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:38.015
If there had been intent to kill, but still no planning,

00:08:38.015 --> 00:08:40.815
then this would have been tried as attempted second-degree murder.

00:08:40.815 --> 00:08:42.380
Regardless, no one dies.

00:08:42.380 --> 00:08:44.960
So does this mean that Daniel gets himself off scot-free?

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:46.360
Absolutely...

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:47.000
not.

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:51.715
For starters, Daniel violated Section 347 of the California Penal Code,

00:08:51.715 --> 00:08:52.620
which states, quote,

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:56.860
"Every person who willfully mingles any poison or harmful substance

00:08:56.860 --> 00:08:59.220
with any food, drink, medicine, or pharmaceutical product

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:01.220
...where the person knows or should have known

00:09:01.220 --> 00:09:04.280
that the same would be taken by any human being to his or her injury,

00:09:04.280 --> 00:09:07.980
is guilty of a felony punishable by imprisonment in the state prison

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:10.525
for two, four, or five years.

00:09:10.525 --> 00:09:14.880
Now clearly, Daniel knew that adding a metric ton of pepper to Stu's dish

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:16.840
would cause him some level of injury.

00:09:16.845 --> 00:09:19.960
So with that, we can add another 5 years to Daniel's sentence.

00:09:19.960 --> 00:09:23.020
Other possible crimes Daniel could be on the hook for here include:

00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:24.000
Reckless endangerment,

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:24.640
battery,

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:26.220
And, on the extreme end,

00:09:26.220 --> 00:09:28.015
Assault with a deadly weapon.

00:09:28.020 --> 00:09:30.320
No, pepper might not *seem* like a deadly weapon,

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:33.000
But since Daniel knew it was harmful to Stu,

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:35.600
a lawyer could absolutely make a case for it.

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:38.320
Which would yield a sentence of up to four years in county jail,

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:40.700
and a fine of 10 thousand dollars.

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:42.315
So between the party violations,

00:09:42.315 --> 00:09:43.080
vandalism,

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:44.180
battery and poisoning,

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:45.980
Daniel Hillard could be facing around

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:48.900
$13,200 in fines.

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:51.720
And an upwards of 10 years in prison.

00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:55.825
As large as that may seem, though, we still haven't touched on his biggest crime.

00:09:55.825 --> 00:09:56.840
Ho-hoh, yeah!

00:09:56.840 --> 00:10:01.540
Almost killing his romantic rival is far from the biggest thing Daniel has to worry about.

00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:04.500
We've overlooked something major up to this point.

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:07.700
So major, in fact, that it could increase Daniel's sentence

00:10:07.700 --> 00:10:09.180
four times over.

00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:11.375
And the thing that I've overlooked up till now,

00:10:11.375 --> 00:10:14.185
is the point of the entire movie.

00:10:14.185 --> 00:10:18.565
You see, according to the terms of divorce announced by the judge at the beginning of the movie,

00:10:18.565 --> 00:10:22.900
Daniel Hillard is only allowed to see his children for a few hours every Saturday.

00:10:22.900 --> 00:10:26.060
For the rest of the week, Miranda has full custody.

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:29.060
Since this divorce agreement is a legal decree,

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:33.075
intentional violation of it is considered contempt of court.

00:10:33.075 --> 00:10:36.220
In order to be convicted of contempt of court in the state of California,

00:10:36.220 --> 00:10:38.800
the defendant must have knowledge about the order in question,

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:41.340
and then have willfully violated that order.

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:44.900
Now, clearly Daniel had knowledge about the divorce agreements.

00:10:44.900 --> 00:10:47.860
Since, he was present in the courtroom when it was decided.

00:10:47.860 --> 00:10:52.335
And the violation of the agreement was absolutely intentional on the part of Daniel.

00:10:52.335 --> 00:10:55.305
It's not like the children happened to see him while he was working at the TV studio,

00:10:55.305 --> 00:10:59.300
Daniel became a nanny expressly to sneak into his former home,

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:00.640
and see his children.

00:11:00.640 --> 00:11:04.185
This is a crystal-clear example of contempt of court.

00:11:04.185 --> 00:11:07.220
Which is punishable by a maximum sentence of 1 year in county jail,

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:08.640
and a thousand dollar fine.

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:09.915
But that's not all!

00:11:09.915 --> 00:11:11.935
For some court orders, including

00:11:11.935 --> 00:11:13.805
Family court matters and restraining orders,

00:11:13.805 --> 00:11:16.985
the California Penal Code mandates that, quote,

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:26.600
This means that each time that Daniel actively saw his kids outside of the court-mandated hours,

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:29.115
is considered a unique offense.

00:11:29.115 --> 00:11:33.440
At the end of the film, it's revealed that it's been two months since the initial divorce hearing.

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:35.000
(Daniel) Your Honor, in the past two months,

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:36.635
I've secured a residence,

00:11:36.635 --> 00:11:37.380
...

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:38.635
I've refurbished that residence,

00:11:38.635 --> 00:11:40.635
and made it an environment fit for children.

00:11:40.635 --> 00:11:42.860
(MatPat) At 5 days a week, for 8 weeks,

00:11:42.860 --> 00:11:47.200
Daniel would be charged with up to 40 cases of contempt of court.

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:50.880
This alone would be upwards of 40 years in jail,

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:53.315
and a $40,000 fine.

00:11:53.315 --> 00:11:55.480
So if you tack on all the other offences,

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:57.840
which look gracious, in comparison now,

00:11:57.840 --> 00:12:02.585
Daniel could potentially be spending nearly 50 years, behind bars.

00:12:02.585 --> 00:12:06.840
And paying over $53,000 in legal fines.

00:12:06.840 --> 00:12:11.680
Now obviously these figures were calculated using the maximum sentencing requirements for each infraction,

00:12:11.680 --> 00:12:15.560
So it is possible that Daniel could have been given a shorter sentencing by the jury,

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:17.625
or received parole for good behavior,

00:12:17.625 --> 00:12:20.940
However, I don't think many jurors and judges are going to be sympathetic

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:22.940
to a man who almost murdered someone,

00:12:22.940 --> 00:12:25.000
while dressed up as an elderly British woman

00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:27.060
So he could sneak into his house and basically

00:12:27.060 --> 00:12:29.445
Kidnap his kids, from a legal standpoint.

00:12:29.445 --> 00:12:31.735
But the worst twist of all,

00:12:31.740 --> 00:12:34.340
is that at the beginning of the movie, it's made clear that:

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:37.640
(Judge) I'm giving you three months, Mr. Hillard. Three months in which to get a job,

00:12:37.735 --> 00:12:39.760
Keep it, and create a suitable home.

00:12:39.760 --> 00:12:41.960
If this proves to be a possibility for you,

00:12:41.960 --> 00:12:45.500
I will consider adjoint custody arrangement when we reconvene.

00:12:45.500 --> 00:12:49.955
All he needed to do was to wait for three months and his problems would have been solved.

00:12:49.955 --> 00:12:53.220
Instead, he self-sabotages yet again.

00:12:53.220 --> 00:12:58.085
This time, actively throwing away the last remaining shred of happiness in his life,

00:12:58.085 --> 00:12:58.940
his kids.

00:12:58.940 --> 00:13:01.680
And because of his actions, the soonest that he'll see them

00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:04.220
is when they're ready to join AARP 
(American Association of Retired Persons).

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:07.240
You can't even claim he was ignorant to all of this.

00:13:07.240 --> 00:13:10.975
Daniel openly recognizes what he's doing halfway through the movie.

00:13:10.975 --> 00:13:14.785
Immediately after revealing his true identity to his kids, Daniel says:

00:13:14.785 --> 00:13:17.800
(Daniel) If she finds out, I'll only be able to see you

00:13:17.800 --> 00:13:20.640
(MatPat) Maybe the best way to see your kids would've been to stay out of the clink,

00:13:20.640 --> 00:13:22.320
ya Mary Poppins reject.

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:26.955
"Mrs. Doubtfire" isn't the happy, family-friendly, inspiring movie that we grew up watching.

00:13:26.955 --> 00:13:32.100
It's about one man systematically, and knowingly destroying the happiness of his life,

00:13:32.100 --> 00:13:33.800
one piece at a time.

00:13:33.800 --> 00:13:34.960
BUT HEY!

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:37.280
That's just a theory,

00:13:37.280 --> 00:13:39.360
A Film Theory.

00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:40.820
Aaaaaaaaaand

00:13:40.820 --> 00:13:41.720
CUT.

00:13:41.720 --> 00:13:42.320
 

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:44.860
Greetings from:
United States Penitentiary
Alcatraz Island
San Francisco, CA.

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:01.500
i'm mary poppins, y'all

